  "result": "Perfect! All 177 tests pass \u2713\n\n**Summary of dates module implementation:**\n\n1. **src/dates.js** \u2014 New module with three utility functions:\n   - `isValidDate(text)` \u2014 Validates date string format (YYYY-MM-DD) and checks if it represents a real date. Rejects impossible dates like 2024-02-30 and non-leap-year Feb 29.\n   - `addDays(date, n)` \u2014 Adds n days to a date string (supports negative n). Works in UTC, handles month/year boundaries and leap years.\n   - `daysBetween(a, b)` \u2014 Calculates whole days between two dates (b minus a). Works in UTC.\n\n2. **Key decisions:**\n   - All date arithmetic is done in UTC, never in local time zone\n   - Uses `T00:00:00Z` to ensure UTC parsing\n   - `addDays` and `daysBetween` return/accept integers for whole days only\n\n3. **src/invoices.js** \u2014 Updated:\n   - Imported `isValidDate` from dates.js\n   - Replaced inline date validation in `createInvoice` with `isValidDate(issueDate)` call\n\n4. **Test coverage** \u2014 22 new tests covering:\n   - Valid dates (including leap years)\n   - Invalid formats (/, wrong order, missing zeros)\n   - Invalid dates (Feb 30, month 13, etc.)\n   - addDays with positive/negative/zero values\n   - addDays crossing month and year boundaries\n   - addDays with leap years\n   - daysBetween with same date, positive, and negative differences\n   - daysBetween crossing boundaries\n   - Round-trip consistency between addDays and daysBetween\n\nAll dates are treated as YYYY-MM-DD strings, parsed and manipulated in UTC, ensuring consistent behavior across all time zones.",
